[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/fastify/issues/comments/1566210671","html_url":"https://github.com/fastify/fastify/issues/4774#issuecomment-1566210671","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/fastify/issues/4774","id":1566210671,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBCRpgs5dWnpv","user":{"login":"metcoder95","id":10200776,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMjAwNzc2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10200776?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95","html_url":"https://github.com/metcoder95","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-05-28T17:45:49Z","updated_at":"2023-05-28T17:45:49Z","body":"Hey! Thanks for the report 🙂 \r\nThe behavior is actually expected, as two things are happening within your example:\r\n\r\n1. Once you trigger `fastify.close` it will start rejecting new connections, and wait until the ones that are open get served before closing the server completely.\r\n2. The `close` callback (and its Promise version) are called once all the `onClose` hooks have been successfully called (if any). This is due to `avvio` behavior which is Fastify extends underneath.\r\n>  __From [Avvio's docs](https://github.com/fastify/avvio#close)__: Starts the shutdown procedure, the callback is called once all the registered callbacks with onClose have been executed.\r\n\r\nI acknowledge that the current [docs](https://www.fastify.io/docs/latest/Reference/Server/#close) does not explain that small point. Maybe something worth it to mention?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/fastify/issues/comments/1566210671/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"metcoder95","id":10200776,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMjAwNzc2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10200776?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95","html_url":"https://github.com/metcoder95","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metcoder95/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/fastify/issues/comments/1566411106","html_url":"https://github.com/fastify/fastify/issues/4774#issuecomment-1566411106","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/fastify/issues/4774","id":1566411106,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBCRpgs5dXYli","user":{"login":"hienngm","id":112270783,"node_id":"U_kgDOBrEdvw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112270783?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hienngm","html_url":"https://github.com/hienngm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hienngm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hienngm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hienngm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hienngm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hienngm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hienngm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hienngm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hienngm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hienngm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-05-29T02:36:11Z","updated_at":"2023-05-29T02:36:11Z","body":"Thank you for your quick response 😄. However, what I meant was `fastify.server.close()` instead of `fastify.close()`. As stated in the Fastify documentation, `fastify.server` returns the underlying Node HTTP server object. Ideally, `fastify.server.close()` should exhibit the same behavior as the raw HTTP server in Node, but it seems to deviate from that behavior which has led to confusion.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/fastify/issues/comments/1566411106/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"hienngm","id":112270783,"node_id":"U_kgDOBrEdvw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112270783?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hienngm","html_url":"https://github.com/hienngm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hienngm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hienngm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hienngm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hienngm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hienngm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hienngm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hienngm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hienngm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hienngm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/fastify/issues/comments/1566672077","html_url":"https://github.com/fastify/fastify/issues/4774#issuecomment-1566672077","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/fastify/issues/4774","id":1566672077,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBCRpgs5dYYTN","user":{"login":"Eomm","id":11404065,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNDA0MDY1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11404065?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eomm","html_url":"https://github.com/Eomm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eomm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eomm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eomm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eomm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eomm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eomm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eomm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eomm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eomm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-05-29T07:15:28Z","updated_at":"2023-05-29T07:15:28Z","body":"In general:\r\n\r\n- prefer `fastify.close()` over `fastify.server.close()` as you are skipping some fastify features (such as the `onClose`)\r\n- in an async handler `return reply` instead of `reply.send()`. It is managed, but it may leads to unpredictable bugs\r\n\r\nIf you run your server with `fastify.listen({ host: '0.0.0.0', port: 3000 }` all will work as expected.\r\n\r\nI think this issue is related to the multiple bindings when we listen to both ipv4 and ipv6 ips\r\n\r\n```\r\n    // https://github.com/nodejs/node/issues/9390\r\n    // If listening to 'localhost', listen to both 127.0.0.1 or ::1 if they are available.\r\n    // If listening to 127.0.0.1, only listen to 127.0.0.1.\r\n    // If listening to ::1, only listen to ::1.\r\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/fastify/issues/comments/1566672077/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"Eomm","id":11404065,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNDA0MDY1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11404065?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eomm","html_url":"https://github.com/Eomm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eomm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eomm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eomm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eomm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eomm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eomm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eomm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eomm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eomm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":9366189336,"node_id":"LE_lADOBCRpgs5nC1HXzwAAAAIuRLUY","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/fastify/issues/events/9366189336","actor":{"login":"Eomm","id":11404065,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNDA0MDY1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11404065?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eomm","html_url":"https://github.com/Eomm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eomm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eomm/fol